--- one function called with a map of ints and a map of floats takes maps
--- of floats, the map of ints converted where it is handed: it had been
--- typed by the second call alone, and the first call's map disagreed with
--- the lowered program (Rosetta Code, Runtime evaluation/In an
--- environment)

fn show[m]
    log[m]

fn total[m]
    return m['x'] + 1

show[map[x = 3]]
show[map[x = 0.5]]
log[total[map[x = 2]], total[map[x = 1.5]]]
